<title>USA: Carbo Ceramics Q1 net per share rises.</title>
<headline>Carbo Ceramics Q1 net per share rises.</headline>
<dateline>IRVING, Texas 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							March 31</p>
<p>						 1997		   1996</p>
<p> Revenues			  $ 17,840,608	  $ 13,032,939</p>
<p> Income before taxes		7,170,075	     4,375,084</p>
<p>Net Income</p>
<p>  (Pro forma for 1996)(a)	 4,586,268	     2,712,552</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding</p>
<p>  (Pro forma for 1996)(b)	14,711,136	    14,602,000</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>  (Pro forma for 1996)		    .31		     .19</p>
<p>(a) Pro forma net income for the three months ended March 31, 1996, reflects a provision for income taxes at an effective rate of 38%.  Prior to April 24, 1996, the Company and its shareholders had elected S Corporation status under the Internal Revenue Code.</p>
<p>(b) Weighted average number of shares for 1997 reflects the issuance of stock options.  Pro forma weighted average number of shares for 1996  represents the number of shares outstanding following the completion of the initial public offering on the company's stock.</p>
<p>Carbo Ceramics Inc.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
